    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d802">

                <pb facs="1082" n="1072" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1072"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50/4–2145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Soong</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-04-20">April 20, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Stetttnius</hi>: Enclosed please find two
                    copies of my memorandum requesting American assistance in meeting our economic
                    difficulties.</p>
                <pb facs="1083" n="1073" xml:id="pg1073"/>
                <p>In discussions which my colleagues have had in the past with the government
                    agencies here, they sometimes found either a failure to appreciate the urgency
                    of the situation or, if they did understand, the fatalistic belief that nothing
                    could be done to hold the line.</p>
                <p>For these reasons, my memorandum is longer than I originally intended, but I hope
                    you will have time to go through it and give it your usual kind assistance.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tse Vun Soong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d802-a1.xml" xpointer="d802-a1"/>
            </div>
